    steps:['Friction depends on how hard the surface pushes up on the object.','Angled up, part of your pull holds up some of the load, so the surface pushes up less. Angled down, part of your push presses the load into the surface.','In the lab, two boxes (35 kg) pulled with 150 N at 30° slide at 1.41 m/s². Pushed with 150 N at 30° down, they do not move at all.'],
