    choices:['It drops to much less than half: from 4.68 to 0.87 m/s²','It drops to exactly half: from 4.68 to 2.34 m/s²','It stays at 4.68 m/s²','It drops to a quarter: from 4.68 to 1.17 m/s²'],correct:0,
    steps:['a = F(cos θ + μk sin θ)/(m₁ + m₂) − μk g.','Doubling the mass halves the first term, from 7.62 to 3.81 m/s², but μk g = 2.94 m/s² stays the same.','So a = 7.62 − 2.94 = 4.68 m/s² becomes 3.81 − 2.94 = 0.87 m/s². Friction grows with the mass; your pull does not.'],
